okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Why Claude Opus 5.5 (released 2026-09-22) does not appear when Claude is launched through ciel-runtime, and the fix."
reported: "User, 2026-09-22: 'ciel-runtime을이용해서 claude를실행시키면 새로나온 모델 opus 5.5등이 안보임'"
status: "Implemented and verified in an isolated run against the live docs page; NOT deployed, and the live router/registry still holds the old list."
confirmed:
  transport: "ciel-runtime's Anthropic list is the docs-page scan intersected with the hand-maintained tuple ANTHROPIC_PUBLIC_MODEL_DEFAULT_IDS (= ANTHROPIC_PUBLIC_MODEL_FALLBACK_IDS) in runtime_constants.py. provider_catalog_sources.filter_anthropic_default_model_ids drops every id outside that tuple, so a model Anthropic ships before the tuple is edited cannot reach any surface: the prelaunch/in-session Model panel, the provider registry, and the router's GET /v1/models (which is what Claude Code's gateway model discovery reads: CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY=1 is set for routed launches)."
  docs_page: "Live fetch of https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview (and the platform.claude.com mirror), 2026-09-22: the public id pattern extracted 21 ids, and claude-opus-5-5 was among them. The allow-list kept 8 (fable-5-1, opus-5, sonnet-5, haiku-4-5-20251001, fable-5, opus-4-8, sonnet-4-6, haiku-4-5) and dropped 13, opus-5-5 first. The page also carries a structured catalog ({\"models\":[{id, lifecycle, legacy, contextWindowTokens, maxOutputTokens, defaultEffort, releasedOn, ...}]}) whose current lineup is fable-5-1, opus-5-5 (releasedOn 2026-09-22, defaultEffort medium, contextWindowTokens 1000000, maxOutputTokens 128000), sonnet-5, haiku-4-5-20251001."
  live_machine: "C:\\Users\\djlov\\AppData\\Roaming\\ciel-runtime\\model-registry.json, anthropic entry: source anthropic-docs, key api=nokey, models = the same 8 ids plus the [1m] customs - no claude-opus-5-5. The running router for this workspace (port 9611, provider deepseek) serves only its current provider's list, so the anthropic list is what a Claude launch would read."
  claude_code_side: "Claude Code's own served catalog cache, ~/.claude/cache/model-catalog/9db340ca-...-cc.json (fetched 2026-09-22 19:13 local), does contain claude-opus-5-5, carrying \"min_claude_code_version\":\"2.1.280\". The installed CLI is 2.1.278 (npm package @anthropic-ai/claude-code), and the CLI binary carries the same field for its bundled fallback entries (\"min_claude_code_version\":\"2.1.251\"). The same cached entry has no fast_mode block while claude-opus-5 and claude-opus-4-8 in that file do, and it marks medium as the default effort."
inferred:
  - "Unverified mechanism: that Claude Code hides a catalog entry whose min_claude_code_version exceeds its own version. The field is present in both the served cache and the bundled catalog and the installed 2.1.278 sits below 5.5's 2.1.280, but the comparison code is not identifiable in the bundled claude.exe. If it holds, a native (direct) Claude launch on 2.1.278 would still not offer Opus 5.5 in Claude Code's own /model picker even with this fix, and the CLI would need updating to 2.1.280+."
  - "The stale registry row is what keeps the old list on screen after the code is fixed: model_panel_rows(fetch=...) fetches only when read_model_list_cache returns None, and model_registry_repository.read_list_cache falls back to registry models of any age, so the anthropic entry has to be refreshed (panel 'Refresh provider model list' or a cleared registry) for the new ids to show."
changes:
  allow_list: "runtime_constants.ANTHROPIC_ONE_MILLION_MODEL_IDS gains claude-opus-5-5[1m]; ANTHROPIC_PUBLIC_MODEL_FALLBACK_IDS (and therefore the default ids) gains claude-opus-5-5."
  lineup_acceptance: "provider_catalog_sources.anthropic_docs_lineup_model_ids parses the page's embedded catalog (marker \\\"models\\\":[, balanced scan, escaped-quote unescape, legacy/lifecycle filtering) and filter_anthropic_default_model_ids accepts those ids on top of the allow-list (limited ids still excluded). The lineup ids also join the scan, so a future family prefix the public id pattern does not cover still appears. Malformed payload -> [] -> allow-list only, as before."
  metadata: "anthropic_model_policy.runtime_hints: explicit claude-opus-5-5 branch ahead of the opus-5 one - default effort medium (published table), no fast_mode (the served catalog lists none for 5.5), adaptive thinking. Limits/capabilities/1M defaults already match through the opus-5 patterns."
  migration: "config_migrations marker anthropic_opus_5_5_1m_model_id_20260922 appends claude-opus-5-5[1m] to an existing anthropic custom_models without touching the selected model."
  docs: "docs/Providers.md explains that the allow-list is an allow-list, not the source of truth."
tests:
  new: "tests/test_provider_catalog_sources.py - lineup parsing (escaped payload, legacy/retired skipped, malformed payload -> []), allow-list lag case, and fetch_anthropic_public_model_ids returning a lineup id outside the allow-list; tests/test_claude_native_provider.py - opus-5-5 in the fallback catalog, 1M limits, medium-effort/no-fast-mode hints."
  updated: "tests/test_runtime_constants.py - opus-5-5 and opus-5-5[1m] presence."
  isolated_run: "C:\\Users\\djlov\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\ciel_opus55_verify.py with CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED=1 and a temp CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR: upstream_model_ids('anthropic', ...) returned 16 ids including claude-opus-5-5 and claude-opus-5-5[1m]; the Model panel rows listed both; the isolated registry recorded source=anthropic-docs with limits 1048576/128000 and runtime hints default_effort=medium."
  groups: "scripts/run_test_group.py: unit 1608 OK (skipped=45), router 1153 OK, channel 423 OK (skipped=80), runtime 296 OK (skipped=19); ruff clean on every touched file."
not_done:
  - "No deploy: the fix lives in the working tree (plus this repo's global install and the pinned snapshot are untouched), so no launched session sees it yet."
  - "The live anthropic registry entry still holds the pre-fix list; the panel will keep showing it until that entry is refreshed or removed."
  - "The min_claude_code_version gate in Claude Code is inferred, not proven; if a native launch is the surface the user meant, the CLI must also move to 2.1.280+."
